<Base lang="hi" title="Certificate time par na mile to kya karein? UP Janhit Guarantee Act 2011 — appeal ka poora tareeqa" description="UP Janhit Guarantee Act 2011 ke tahat certificate deri par pehli appeal SDM aur doosri appeal DM ke paas — 30 aur 60 din ki limit, jurmana, revision aur poora tareeqa।" path="/blog/janhit-guarantee-appeal-delayed-certificate/" altPath="/en/" faqs={faqs} updated="6 नवंबर 2026" datePublished="2026-11-06" dateModified="2026-11-06">
<div class="content-col"><h1 class="page-title">Certificate time par na mile to kya karein?</h1>
<p class="note">नोट: यह वेबसाइट एक स्वतंत्र जानकारी गाइड है — इसका आधिकारिक पोर्टल edistrict.up.gov.in से कोई संबंध नहीं है। यह article jaankari ke liye hai, kanooni salah nahi।</p>
<p>Income, caste ya domicile certificate ke liye aavedan kiya, lekin hafte guzar gaye aur status wahi ka wahi hai? UP me is ka jawab sirf "intezar karein" nahi hai — <strong>UP Janhit Guarantee Act, 2011</strong> ke tahat aapko service tay time me milne ka haq hai, aur deri par appeal karne ka rasta bhi hai।</p>
<section class="box"><h2>Act kya hai</h2><p>Uttar Pradesh Janhit Guarantee Adhiniyam, 2011 — 14 जनवरी 2011 se lagu — kehta hai ke sarkari sevayein tay time limit me milni chahiye। Agar aavedan reject ho jaye ya tay time me service na mile to aap appeal kar sakte hain। Act ki Section 6 me appeal ka tareeqa, Section 7 me jurmane ka rule aur Section 8 me revision ka provision likha hai। Ye kanoon is liye bana tha ke aam aadmi ko apne kaam ke liye daftar ke chakkar na lagane padein aur har service ki ek tay had ho।</p></section>
<section class="box"><h2>Act ke main hisse</h2><ul><li><strong>Section 3 — Services notify hoti hain:</strong> sarkar notification se tay karti hai ke kaun si service, kitne din me, kaun se officer (designated officer) se milegi — aur pehla appeal officer aur doosri appeal wali authority kaun hogi।</li><li><strong>Section 4 — Time par service ka haq:</strong> har nagrik ko notified service tay time me milne ka haq hai।</li><li><strong>Section 5 — Time par dena:</strong> designated officer ko service tay time me deni hoti hai।</li><li><strong>Section 6 — Appeal:</strong> rejection ya time limit khatam hone par pehli appeal 30 din me, aur us ke faisle par doosri appeal 60 din me।</li><li><strong>Section 7 — Jurmana:</strong> appeal time par decide na karne par pehle appeal officer par ₹500–₹5,000 jurmana।</li><li><strong>Section 8 — Revision:</strong> jurmane ke order se naraz officer 60 din me nominated officer ke paas revision ke liye ja sakta hai।</li></ul></section>
<section class="box"><h2>Appeal ka rasta — caste certificate ki misaal</h2><p>Allahabad High Court ke 2023–2024 ke faislon me caste certificate ke liye ye chain confirm hua hai:</p><table class="data"><thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Kahan</th><th>Kab tak</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Aavedan</td><td>Tehsildar (pehla officer)</td><td>Faisla ~20 din me</td></tr><tr><td>Pehli appeal</td><td>SDM</td><td>Rejection ya time limit khatam hone ke 30 din ke andar; faisla 30 din me</td></tr><tr><td>Doosri appeal</td><td>DM (District Magistrate)</td><td>Pehli appeal ke faisle ke 60 din ke andar</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="note">Har service ki time limit alag hoti hai — apni service ki limit service-specific notification se verify karein।</div></section>
<section class="box"><h2>Ek misaal — poori timeline</h2><p>Samajhne ke liye ek misaal lein — caste certificate ke liye, court ke bataye hue 20 din ke hisaab se:</p><ol><li><strong>1 नवंबर:</strong> aapne Tehsildar ke paas caste certificate ke liye aavedan kiya।</li><li><strong>21 नवंबर tak:</strong> faisla aana chahiye tha — lekin koi jawab nahi aaya।</li><li><strong>21 दिसंबर tak:</strong> aap SDM ke paas pehli appeal kar sakte hain — time limit khatam hone ke 30 din ke andar।</li><li><strong>SDM ka faisla:</strong> pehli appeal ka faisla 30 din me hona chahiye।</li><li><strong>Agar SDM bhi faisla na karein ya appeal reject kar dein:</strong> to un ke faisle ke 60 din ke andar DM ke paas doosri appeal kar sakte hain।</li></ol><p>Ye misaal sirf samjhane ke liye hai — asal dates aapke aavedan ki submission date aur service ki notified time limit se tay hongi।</p></section>
<section class="box"><h2>Appeal me kya likhein</h2><p>Appeal likhte waqt ye cheezein saaf taur par likhein:</p><ul class="checklist"><li>Service ka naam — kis certificate ke liye aavedan kiya tha।</li><li>Application / SRN number aur submission ki date।</li><li>Rejection ki wajah (agar reject hua ho) ya time limit kab khatam hui।</li><li>Aap kya chahte hain — certificate jari karne ka order।</li><li>Supporting documents — receipt, status ka screenshot, rejection letter (agar ho)।</li><li>Apna naam, pata aur mobile number — taake faisle ki khabar mil sake।</li></ul></section>
<section class="box"><h2>Jurmana bhi hai</h2><p>Act ki Section 7 ke mutabiq, agar pehla appeal officer bina kaafi wajah ke appeal tay time me decide na kare to doosri appeal wali authority us par <strong>₹500 se ₹5,000 tak jurmana</strong> laga sakti hai। Ye rule is liye hai ke appeal bhi latkaya na jaye। Aur Section 8 ke tahat jurmane ke order par revision bhi ho sakti hai — naraz officer 60 din me nominated officer ke paas ja sakta hai।</p></section>
<section class="box"><h2>Appeal vs shikayat — farq samjhein</h2><p>Dono alag raste hain aur dono ka apna kaam hai:</p><ul><li><strong>Shikayat (grievance):</strong> IGRS portal ya CM Helpline <strong>1076</strong> par shikayat darj karna — ye mamle ko uthata hai aur jawab mangta hai, lekin ye kanooni appeal nahi hai।</li><li><strong>Appeal:</strong> Janhit Guarantee Act ke tahat kanooni rasta — is me officer ko faisla karna hota hai, aur na karne par jurmana bhi lag sakta hai।</li></ul><p>Aam taur par pehle shikayat karke dekhein — aksar mamla wahin sulajh jata hai। Agar na suljhe aur time limit guzar jaye to appeal ka rasta khula hai। Shikayat karne se appeal ka haq khatam nahi hota, lekin appeal ki dates ka dhyaan rakhein — 30 aur 60 din ki limit submission ya faisle ki date se chalti hai।</p></section>
<section class="box"><h2>Appeal se pehle ye karein</h2><ul class="checklist"><li>Application / SRN number, receipt aur submission ki date sambhal kar rakhein।</li><li><a href="/status-verification/">स्टेटस चेक</a> karke remark padhein — rejection ki wajah wahin likhi hoti hai।</li><li>Helpdesk <strong>0522-2304706</strong> ya CM Helpline <strong>1076</strong> par shikayat darj karein aur complaint number lein।</li><li>Rejection letter ya status ka screenshot save rakhein — appeal me kaam aayega।</li><li>Deadline wale documents (admission / bharti notice) ho to saath attach karein।</li></ul><div class="warn">Time limit ka khaas dhyaan rakhein — pehli appeal 30 din aur doosri appeal 60 din me karni hoti hai। Der ho jaye to kaafi wajah batani hogi, aur officer maan bhi sakta hai aur nahi bhi।</div></section>
